              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tim Gonzalez-Wiler"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These meatballs are DELICIOUS, but very greasy. And it's hard to not burn them at the temperature suggested. My thermometer said 275 degrees, and I still couldn't get them both cooked through and not burned. I baked the second half of the batch at about 400 degrees for maybe 30 minutes. I also didn't have any parsley or lemon. I'm excited to include those ingredients next time.",
